<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [1205].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>1205&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;FUNDIDESULFOVIBRIO MAGNETOTACTCUS MEDIUM</FONT></B></P>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> NH<sub>4</sub>Cl                                                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> MgSO<sub>4</sub>&#183;7H<sub>2</sub>O                                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Modified Wolfe's mineral solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=915">915</a>)   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Casamino acids (BD-Difco)                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Yeast extract                                           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.02&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Resazurin                                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;957.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components thoroughly, adjust pH to 7.0 and autoclave under a N<sub>2</sub> gas atmosphere.  After cooling, aseptically and anaerobically add the following solutions from anaerobic stocks (autoclaved or *filter-sterilized):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 0.25 M Potassium phosphate buffer (pH 7.0)              </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.6&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Vitamin solution* (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=915">915</a>)                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% L-Cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O solution (pH 7.0)   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;8.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 10 mM Fe quinate solution* (see below)                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Distribute the medium into culture vessels (e.g., 20 ml in Balch tubes) and seal with butyl rubber stoppers.  <br>
10mM Fe quinate solution:  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> FeCl<sub>3</sub>&#183;6H<sub>2</sub>O   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.225  &nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g   </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Quinic acid   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.095  &nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g   </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;50.0 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml    </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Comment:  <br>
JCM 32405 may grow better in a modified medium by the addition of 20 mM sodium lactate and 50 μM Fe(III)•EDTA instead of casamino acids and ferric quinate. However, formation of magnetosomes in cells may be inhibited in the modified medium.       <br>
